# Cosmai secret store — key names and formats.
#
# This file is committed to Git and records NAMES only. Never put a real value here.
#
# The real store lives outside the repository working tree, by default at
# ~/.config/cosmai/env (mode 600), and uses the same KEY=VALUE syntax.
# Run commands through the launcher, which validates the store and exports its
# path as COSMA_SECRET_SOURCE:
#
#   ./scripts/with-secret-source.sh <command>
#
# Credential values are never exported into the process environment. They are
# read from the store at the point of use.
#
# Procedure: docs/conventions/secret-setup.md
# Constraint: docs/conventions/p0-security.md

# --- Credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Naming: COSMA_SRC_<SOURCE_ID>_<PURPOSE>
#
# The `credential_ref` persisted in the database is exactly this key name. The
# value is never stored in a source row, job payload, Raw envelope, log, or
# fixture. Which refs a worker may resolve is open — see OQ-007.
#
# COSMA_SRC_EXAMPLE_TOKEN=<opaque bearer token>
# COSMA_SRC_EXAMPLE_API_KEY=<api key>

# --- Values that embed a credential ------------------------------------------
#
# A connection string carrying a password is a credential. Store it here by key
# and resolve it through `credential_ref`; do not pass it as an environment
# variable. Non-credential local configuration does not belong in this store.
#
# COSMA_DB_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/cosmai
